  "kind": "help-article",
  "title": "NSS Feed Output Format: Event Logs",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://help.zscaler.com/cloud-branch-connector/nss-feed-output-format-event-logs",
    "node": "1459131",
    "revision": "3220457",
    "updated": "2026-08-13",
    "updated_basis": "pdf-last-modified"
  },
  "captured_at": "2026-10-19",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "The Event NSS feed specifies the data from the Event logs that the Nanolog Streaming Service (NSS) sends to the security information and event management (SIEM) system. You can configure an NSS feed by including one or more fields. The fields and their values display in the NSS feed output."
    },
    {
      "text": "Zscaler Cloud Connector or Branch Connector generates the Event logs when a status change occurs for a Cloud Connector or Branch Connector health check, Zscaler data center reachability, a data plane health check, a software upgrade, a control plane health check, or a tunnel to Zscaler data centers."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Event Log Attributes",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Each Event log has date and time, metadata, and event-specific attributes in it. The event-specific attributes depend on the type and severity of the event. Therefore, the values of the attributes change depending on the event type and severity."
    },
    {
      "text": "There are 9 event-specific attributes in each Event log:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 1 Type: The data type for the first event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 1 Value: The value for the first event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 2 Type: The data type for the second event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 2 Value: The value for the second event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 3 Type: The data type for the third event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 3 Value: The value for the third event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 4 Type: The data type for the fourth event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute 4 Value: The value for the fourth event attribute.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Error Code: The error code associated with an event if an error code is available.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
